From: Christopher Owen <3221756+christopherowen@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sun, 25 Oct 2026 17:10:56 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] Model loading: a weight digest on every rank
 (SPARK_DS41F_WEIGHT_DIGEST)

A debug check for comparing checkpoint loaders. With
SPARK_DS41F_WEIGHT_DIGEST=1, BaseModelLoader.load_model hashes every
parameter's bytes in name order (a shared parameter once) right after
load_weights, before post-load processing turns them into kernel layouts,
and each rank logs

  weight digest rank <rank> <sha256> <model class>: <n> parameters, ...

A speculative model loads through the same loader and logs its own line.
The bytes pass through one 64 MiB host buffer; the CPU's SHA-256 adds some
tens of seconds to a DS4.1 rank's start. Unset (production), it reads the
variable once at import and does nothing else.

Tests (no GPU): name order at any staging size, strided parameters in
logical order, FP8/BF16/bool/0-d parameters, one flipped bit, meta
parameters refused, the logged line matched by the lab's loader report,
and the digest's place between loading and processing.
